      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-43981",
      ":question/problem": "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nGiven the functions $f(t)=t$ and $g(t)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9=2\\pi $\n- $\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9=0$\n- $f(t)\u22a5g(t)$ with respect to the inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ in $V$"
