      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-97451",
      ":question/problem": "Let $V=C[0,2\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(t)g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nGiven the functions $f(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$ and $g(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3t),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9=0$\n- $\u27e8f(t),g(t)\u27e9=2\\pi $\n- $f(t)\u22a5g(t)$ with respect to the inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ in $V$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the identity $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\beta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\alpha +\\beta )).$*"
